  'Page Layout (InDesign)',
  'Page Layout (InDesign)',
  'Page Layout (InDesign) develops the technical, visual, and production judgment required to design professional publications for print and digital delivery. Students learn InDesign through editorial design problems: grids, typography, multi-page systems, image placement, styles, parent pages, tables, preflight, packaging, accessible exports, and critique-driven revision. The course culminates in a polished publication system that can function as a portfolio case study.',
  $pagljson${"slug": "page-layout-indesign", "title": "Page Layout (InDesign)", "description": "Page Layout (InDesign) develops the technical, visual, and production judgment required to design professional publications for print and digital delivery. Students learn InDesign through editorial design problems: grids, typography, multi-page systems, image placement, styles, parent pages, tables, preflight, packaging, accessible exports, and critique-driven revision. The course culminates in a polished publication system that can function as a portfolio case study.", "topics": [{"id": "ef1d4b84-5c8c-49eb-a8ca-c21694fda7f4", "type": "topic", "title": "Page Layout as Editorial Communication and Publication Systems", "description": "This opening unit frames page layout as communication design, not merely software operation. Students learn how editorial intent, audience, sequence, hierarchy, and production context shape every page decision.", "children": [{"id": "35408ba3-4914-4317-ae1d-9aa86980f0d5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Editorial purpose and audience", "children": [{"id": "6fc700a4-1c04-4813-bdcd-1333403e672d", "type": "concept", "title": "reader needs and publication goals"}, {"id": "b2d062dd-e3a0-447f-8ddf-9b66adce3def", "type": "concept", "title": "tone, genre, and brand voice"}, {"id": "46971df6-f94c-4303-bd53-55f6d0ebd9b1", "type": "concept", "title": "editorial hierarchy and sequencing"}, {"id": "0a0a7195-2bdb-48fc-a994-c62f998b30f3", "type": "concept", "title": "content audits and page inventories"}], "description": "Students learn to translate content goals into layout choices that make reading purposeful, credible, and visually memorable."}, {"id": "40a37444-0cdf-47cc-836e-0c269decd632", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Publication systems thinking", "children": [{"id": "da84c483-0883-4fa6-a52b-0752ce33aa82", "type": "concept", "title": "recurring page types"}, {"id": "4e6cb01e-b61a-4448-8e71-d7106bd20c12", "type": "concept", "title": "section rhythm"}, {"id": "c34d7ac9-2719-4fd8-8ba9-26bb6e89851c", "type": "concept", "title": "template logic"}, {"id": "0a1245a4-8f32-4608-9c54-2b7b28dee2f1", "type": "concept", "title": "cross-document consistency"}], "description": "The goal is to see a brochure, report, magazine, or book as a repeatable system rather than a set of isolated pages."}, {"id": "1545dcb5-246c-42e6-b243-0e8e42535f16", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Visual communication ethics", "children": [{"id": "d46d233e-d733-4a14-ad69-45ead809c403", "type": "concept", "title": "legibility and accessibility"}, {"id": "edbe0fa8-96d4-436e-8f24-464c2c3daaa7", "type": "concept", "title": "image context and captions"}, {"id": "19b657bb-6747-48aa-8746-61f756c4bf5e", "type": "concept", "title": "data and quote integrity"}, {"id": "8cd969d3-73ba-4b12-a91c-5a3e185a1cfb", "type": "concept", "title": "inclusive representation"}], "description": "Layout can clarify, persuade, include, or mislead; this subtopic establishes responsible design habits early."}]}, {"id": "42cf3747-d8a0-4fbf-b942-ef83c6e4f9c0", "type": "topic", "title": "InDesign Workspace, File Structure, and Professional Workflow", "description": "Students build confidence in the InDesign environment while learning the file habits used in studios, agencies, publishers, and in-house creative teams.", "children": [{"id": "42f56fe4-86b5-4853-a788-82248dbfe135", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Workspace fluency", "children": [{"id": "221c971f-4a06-452e-9947-f8df94b662b2", "type": "concept", "title": "tools, panels, and control bar"}, {"id": "ef498f0d-2458-4c8c-9126-87f57e5c20fc", "type": "concept", "title": "workspace presets"}, {"id": "f1a673ee-6134-4856-ba23-256322569197", "type": "concept", "title": "rulers, guides, and smart guides"}, {"id": "0a1d2a76-87d3-4420-a6be-7f2c8e02e887", "type": "concept", "title": "shortcuts and command search"}], "description": "Students learn where tools live, how panels work, and how to customize the interface so production decisions stay fast and accurate."}, {"id": "e47810dc-3759-485f-8744-c3d5aea5bc03", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Document and project organization", "children": [{"id": "b8558be4-8e68-43d5-9d96-44bd20d39731", "type": "concept", "title": "folder structures"}, {"id": "4770e82c-8d76-400a-8cc5-8eb9fbf0fbb8", "type": "concept", "title": "naming and versioning"}, {"id": "183c29eb-ec4f-45c3-8888-5b780d6e0ba1", "type": "concept", "title": "links and fonts folders"}, {"id": "46cb18d4-0ba6-43b9-a37f-c30adeffb6c9", "type": "concept", "title": "asset checklists"}], "description": "A good layout file is supported by clean folders, linked assets, naming conventions, and predictable exports."}, {"id": "62be3943-365c-4bb8-8dcf-97577c95963d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Cross-app workflow", "children": [{"id": "3fb741c5-20d9-4d8a-adbf-04cb57eb4767", "type": "concept", "title": "PSD, AI, SVG, PDF, and image formats"}, {"id": "7cb6cf95-6996-498d-ba74-694585390cfd", "type": "concept", "title": "linked versus embedded assets"}, {"id": "10cbb722-4ca6-4426-8d03-2027e6c99d11", "type": "concept", "title": "Creative Cloud Libraries"}, {"id": "7408e126-0ccd-408f-b8ba-fe3f492d424a", "type": "concept", "title": "handoff to Acrobat and print vendors"}], "description": "InDesign often depends on Photoshop, Illustrator, Acrobat, and font services, so students learn how assets move across the Adobe ecosystem."}]}, {"id": "fa47fa6a-3cb1-4a9c-8a70-40c8e8c09123", "type": "topic", "title": "Document Setup: Pages, Spreads, Bleeds, Margins, and Columns", "description": "This unit teaches students to set up a document correctly before designing, preventing common production failures and helping layouts feel intentional from the first page.", "children": [{"id": "ff072bfd-0b36-465e-a7ac-dabdbbe7f79e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Page formats and publication specs", "children": [{"id": "cf202b92-f6f4-4eea-b940-a246aed56174", "type": "concept", "title": "trim size and orientation"}, {"id": "3b0b279e-8890-4917-9c06-c8a091d91f3f", "type": "concept", "title": "facing pages and spreads"}, {"id": "26af445c-acc1-4bcd-94ea-e1ca4fbf4023", "type": "concept", "title": "slug, bleed, and safe area"}, {"id": "11661174-1630-44d9-868d-4845ce8cd75f", "type": "concept", "title": "print versus screen dimensions"}], "description": "Students learn how physical and digital formats affect page size, orientation, spread behavior, and output planning."}, {"id": "2496e619-b944-42f4-8738-956b7224bb37", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Margins, columns, and baseline grids", "children": [{"id": "be72a9d9-f093-41e7-b957-a07d4e51ff37", "type": "concept", "title": "margin systems"}, {"id": "020db851-e9f9-4201-a38a-0052d3323459", "type": "concept", "title": "column count and gutters"}, {"id": "933e5d1f-7abd-4700-9ac3-cf8892481dd5", "type": "concept", "title": "baseline grid setup"}, {"id": "474626c4-90f9-405b-b45a-34550507cdc0", "type": "concept", "title": "modular spacing units"}], "description": "Students use structural guides to turn content into readable systems with strong alignment and rhythm."}, {"id": "845ecefa-a9a1-4549-a5e8-672303de9b99", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Document presets and templates", "children": [{"id": "0f2eea28-bafe-48e2-9023-2393ebf3521e", "type": "concept", "title": "custom presets"}, {"id": "7167590d-03a0-4531-b688-0a1b2c3e94e3", "type": "concept", "title": "template files"}, {"id": "b63bb2ff-4ed7-45b2-882f-a27d14951af7", "type": "concept", "title": "page count planning"}, {"id": "7db62728-208f-4abd-a4d7-5548360c1281", "type": "concept", "title": "default styles and swatches"}], "description": "Students learn to save setup decisions so future projects begin with reliable production foundations."}]}, {"id": "36d14336-31e3-4d1f-a7c5-b1ef7b085cd3", "type": "topic", "title": "Grids, Guides, Modular Systems, and Spatial Hierarchy", "description": "Grid systems turn pages into organized fields. Students learn when to follow a grid, when to bend it, and how hierarchy emerges from structure.", "children": [{"id": "9c6c3d9a-1a91-4142-a316-c2ef4da92e27", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Classical and modern grid systems", "children": [{"id": "e9258a1c-b097-45cb-bcf3-98683f18d834", "type": "concept", "title": "manuscript grids"}, {"id": "3e26ad38-01c0-40ac-a0aa-a90fd5d05b20", "type": "concept", "title": "column grids"}, {"id": "23d6b8d9-5d35-40be-a4c5-dd579cb0cc12", "type": "concept", "title": "modular grids"}, {"id": "1dcee48e-b5ad-4f4a-a7f2-543bc1afa2c9", "type": "concept", "title": "Swiss and contemporary grid traditions"}], "description": "Students study single-column, multicolumn, modular, manuscript, and asymmetric grids as tools for clarity and variation."}, {"id": "cf82c936-cbc1-4720-b831-f450f96675b1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Hierarchy through space", "children": [{"id": "f3a254bc-34f5-481c-9322-a30524f167ec", "type": "concept", "title": "visual entry points"}, {"id": "3dd4314d-dc5d-49ff-b772-73d56e94b262", "type": "concept", "title": "proximity and grouping"}, {"id": "c438ed21-71ea-4840-b2af-34fd6772441f", "type": "concept", "title": "white space as structure"}, {"id": "3efcb160-a676-41ef-a8ba-7b349f727c1e", "type": "concept", "title": "rhythm across spreads"}], "description": "Students learn to use scale, grouping, whitespace, and alignment to signal what matters first, second, and third."}, {"id": "ec163234-8d9f-4884-be27-0bc72ac562b4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Breaking the grid", "children": [{"id": "73542f62-4a91-4776-aa41-90d5e533d187", "type": "concept", "title": "intentional asymmetry"}, {"id": "2e65ea9d-cfa2-40c5-a56a-6033fc39d7c8", "type": "concept", "title": "overlap and layering"}, {"id": "930ea286-35d9-4534-b491-5643c6d13e58", "type": "concept", "title": "scale contrast"}, {"id": "f3bb88df-9cbf-4a69-9f66-38be5588f3d2", "type": "concept", "title": "editorial pacing"}], "description": "Students practice controlled disruption so expressive pages remain readable and purposeful."}]}, {"id": "901a99a2-de73-46e4-9654-c6ef6186cb5c", "type": "topic", "title": "Text Frames, Image Frames, Linking, Fitting, and Layout Objects", "description": "This unit moves from setup into page construction. Students learn the core mechanics of building layouts with text, image, and object frames.", "children": [{"id": "7c2aa40c-8230-4dd1-990e-2f5257e6673a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Text frame control", "children": [{"id": "bb23b6cc-780b-46cf-a2c3-21302b3a120a", "type": "concept", "title": "threaded text"}, {"id": "8f74ccc4-d205-402e-8706-c137d51cd38f", "type": "concept", "title": "inset spacing"}, {"id": "066477c6-ee1c-48e7-a7c0-7d4e6aaca4a9", "type": "concept", "title": "columns inside frames"}, {"id": "015285f2-680f-47fb-af19-9f045d1fec91", "type": "concept", "title": "overset text warnings"}], "description": "Students learn how text behaves inside InDesign and how threaded frames support multi-page reading."}, {"id": "54f3416c-18af-446b-8850-dc91acdb0b5c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Image placement and fitting", "children": [{"id": "7d473197-42ef-4e38-999e-672b4592b339", "type": "concept", "title": "frame fitting options"}, {"id": "013303e8-00fe-4590-80cf-48af86d2a99c", "type": "concept", "title": "content-aware fit"}, {"id": "088035a1-6d7d-439d-a178-6b816c08f423", "type": "concept", "title": "effective resolution"}, {"id": "e8e9998c-1ca3-4ab2-bf75-abd852a1e55d", "type": "concept", "title": "captions and credit lines"}], "description": "Students learn to place, crop, scale, and align images without damaging quality or breaking links."}, {"id": "6a8e4537-16a4-44f1-8bbe-d60e931f7b55", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Objects, layers, and alignment", "children": [{"id": "bf91520d-4037-45de-9ea6-8aafed1083fb", "type": "concept", "title": "object stacking"}, {"id": "74c0e22a-d2e1-4483-8d36-1d31fa86ba09", "type": "concept", "title": "alignment tools"}, {"id": "76df6575-712d-4cc0-a100-ee38ee0a72fd", "type": "concept", "title": "text wrap"}, {"id": "926f53ca-4a46-4286-b858-6b97f40deb2b", "type": "concept", "title": "layer naming and locking"}], "description": "Students manage shapes, rules, objects, and layers so layouts stay editable and orderly."}]}, {"id": "ae09951c-7cd1-4339-93d6-284d8bb4ada1", "type": "topic", "title": "Typography for Layout: Hierarchy, Readability, Styles, and Long-Form Text", "description": "Typography is the spine of page layout. Students develop type judgment for headlines, bodies, captions, tables, and long-form editorial systems.", "children": [{"id": "4afeb1ed-e0f4-4e30-983b-161f17354e23", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Type hierarchy and voice", "children": [{"id": "5242fbde-535c-4433-aaf9-f40e93633db2", "type": "concept", "title": "display, text, and utility faces"}, {"id": "c2c995a5-445d-4484-ada2-0af930417ad9", "type": "concept", "title": "type pairing"}, {"id": "b8c4816e-2a61-4573-992e-6597a6d92559", "type": "concept", "title": "scale systems"}, {"id": "7a9a02a4-2c2d-4323-8feb-23702f07b9bc", "type": "concept", "title": "typographic contrast"}], "description": "Students learn to choose and combine typefaces so the publication has a clear tone and a readable order."}, {"id": "3f7f42f2-f13c-4481-98a7-cb312565175e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Readability and spacing", "children": [{"id": "73f4f5f9-f68b-4806-a65c-186010679824", "type": "concept", "title": "leading, tracking, and kerning"}, {"id": "a1193e3c-5bd1-462f-95eb-c27b54d73d4e", "type": "concept", "title": "measure and line length"}, {"id": "9d1b7c06-3e08-4d18-b56a-95f8d25c3077", "type": "concept", "title": "paragraph spacing"}, {"id": "b83e26bf-c1f2-4f25-80de-8739d00dfee5", "type": "concept", "title": "widows, orphans, and rivers"}], "description": "Students tune type so reading feels effortless across short and long documents."}, {"id": "165c4a31-5012-4e0e-a5fb-7c61b7863bad", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Long-form text systems", "children": [{"id": "9fbc9585-b06d-4172-b4ce-941a5625f88f", "type": "concept", "title": "threaded stories"}, {"id": "b73edf36-8819-4677-b8ce-cffac59f9e0a", "type": "concept", "title": "columns and text flow"}, {"id": "dc65933c-90b5-4deb-9238-1bc92d3ea4df", "type": "concept", "title": "hyphenation and justification"}, {"id": "e04e3c9a-5387-4dea-96e9-70ca53e6a5b6", "type": "concept", "title": "footnotes, endnotes, and running headers"}], "description": "Students learn the features that make books, reports, and magazines manageable."}]}, {"id": "ce8a362d-6c73-4726-8ee7-df25af6c8669", "type": "topic", "title": "Paragraph, Character, Object, Table, and Master/Parent Page Styles", "description": "Styles are the bridge between design and production. Students learn to make documents consistent, fast to revise, and easier to hand off.", "children": [{"id": "59d06136-3117-4b59-bbbb-3646818ad635", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Paragraph and character styles", "children": [{"id": "6fa68e9b-eb70-41f4-98d6-7ce427db4ace", "type": "concept", "title": "style hierarchy"}, {"id": "9ab82079-2a30-424e-9895-43ff0613eab8", "type": "concept", "title": "nested and GREP styles"}, {"id": "363e9ab1-1768-4cbb-9f52-7385dab82504", "type": "concept", "title": "based-on relationships"}, {"id": "696190f9-d607-45c6-bb43-624c9af137f3", "type": "concept", "title": "style overrides and cleanup"}], "description": "Students create reusable type rules so formatting is systematic instead of manual."}, {"id": "e72fafde-3761-42e0-82c5-63ec5f85f130", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Object, table, and cell styles", "children": [{"id": "188977ad-1eea-44e9-95b3-432adb759a7d", "type": "concept", "title": "object style defaults"}, {"id": "b6590a35-c211-4d71-b116-2e7b676faf5b", "type": "concept", "title": "table headers and body cells"}, {"id": "78ee8847-8347-4ecb-80c3-3da0b7a52f36", "type": "concept", "title": "caption frames"}, {"id": "c3c8e4c2-dced-4561-affb-989710e760f7", "type": "concept", "title": "rule and callout styling"}], "description": "Students extend consistency beyond type into frames, tables, rules, and recurring page elements."}, {"id": "45dfce12-1deb-4526-a3ac-85cb7e13d996", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Parent pages and master systems", "children": [{"id": "99ede377-8e6b-4731-8a40-b64fec2e7082", "type": "concept", "title": "folios and running heads"}, {"id": "c5f1a9b0-4202-481f-b3cf-281086fa3413", "type": "concept", "title": "section markers"}, {"id": "2c070496-d92e-4af1-ab8b-70fce4f4538e", "type": "concept", "title": "automatic page numbering"}, {"id": "30be43cd-a624-40ef-b451-1aada11afe0e", "type": "concept", "title": "parent page overrides"}], "description": "Students learn how recurring layout elements control page identity while allowing local variation."}]}, {"id": "4abef52a-e3bf-47ab-8401-405138d21251", "type": "topic", "title": "Image Preparation, Resolution, Color Modes, and Linked Asset Management", "description": "Strong layout depends on production-ready images. Students learn how resolution, color, compression, and file linking affect final output quality.", "children": [{"id": "32b64ba0-27c0-4ddc-b6c5-1f1f5dc38361", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Raster image preparation", "children": [{"id": "064a6b8c-77c2-4549-863c-6aa29890f530", "type": "concept", "title": "ppi and effective resolution"}, {"id": "a4d0f09b-51f3-4240-8434-0427ab3cd541", "type": "concept", "title": "cropping and sharpening"}, {"id": "bf8f5723-c25d-4759-8412-d976a464c7f1", "type": "concept", "title": "retouching boundaries"}, {"id": "1d426f82-4b64-423c-aa91-3ade7e18ec5e", "type": "concept", "title": "PSD, TIFF, JPEG, and PNG choices"}], "description": "Students learn the Photoshop-facing skills needed to deliver clean, correctly sized imagery."}, {"id": "57b8d3d2-5f70-45c3-a71b-b4cc90c6e6c1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Vector and illustration assets", "children": [{"id": "3da52a03-d2a9-4985-a420-58433e5fac71", "type": "concept", "title": "AI and PDF placement"}, {"id": "9bf8dbe1-59d0-4376-b8a9-64f015b5b942", "type": "concept", "title": "logos and icons"}, {"id": "d9c6b32f-9065-4c33-82c3-ecf4dd7a922a", "type": "concept", "title": "spot colors and swatches"}, {"id": "2a179dbc-0486-4eeb-b0d4-26fc85570ad7", "type": "concept", "title": "scalable diagrams"}], "description": "Students learn when Illustrator assets should remain vector and how to import them without losing editability or clarity."}, {"id": "8b9aa7b6-dec2-439d-ad5c-44235098854d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Color management and asset integrity", "children": [{"id": "5d618e51-83db-4d7d-aa0d-bc6a676d7674", "type": "concept", "title": "RGB, CMYK, and spot color"}, {"id": "c4ddcbb1-3afe-44e5-aaac-13dc9fbc6c4a", "type": "concept", "title": "ICC profiles"}, {"id": "f60ea2c0-7c07-40aa-82a3-fb543628aa93", "type": "concept", "title": "link relinking and updates"}, {"id": "8cc01e93-3b77-4b30-85d8-4733fbd04f50", "type": "concept", "title": "missing fonts and missing links"}], "description": "Students learn how profiles, swatches, and links protect color and quality through the production chain."}]}, {"id": "67c5eb9a-3c91-4c2f-934b-b2958ac9ec62", "type": "topic", "title": "Multi-Page Editorial Design: Covers, TOCs, Sections, and Navigation", "description": "Students move from individual pages to full publications. The focus is pacing, navigation, and consistency across covers, front matter, sections, and endings.", "children": [{"id": "6f5ba902-b14f-45ad-811e-a37ca1df0f99", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Publication architecture", "children": [{"id": "db2031cb-e273-4c85-9252-50a0de56ebe1", "type": "concept", "title": "cover and back cover roles"}, {"id": "ac857edf-3b73-4f60-a266-06c5bdfba7bf", "type": "concept", "title": "front matter"}, {"id": "873181cd-96b2-47dd-ba35-8e68aa9ada83", "type": "concept", "title": "table of contents"}, {"id": "72281726-e676-4920-88db-71eb8190702f", "type": "concept", "title": "section openers and departments"}], "description": "Students plan how readers enter, move through, and leave a publication."}, {"id": "dbea6feb-5787-416c-a5e9-dee967e24f42", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Editorial pacing", "children": [{"id": "e43947b1-1c87-4390-b437-8fe1b37f03e7", "type": "concept", "title": "feature openers"}, {"id": "c890462b-39dd-4bcb-8981-254e1eea37b1", "type": "concept", "title": "short versus long reads"}, {"id": "602ac06c-0898-48a6-8941-a4938a13fac3", "type": "concept", "title": "visual pauses"}, {"id": "53011ee2-4f94-4583-b45b-fc1fa5eeeb12", "type": "concept", "title": "sequence and surprise"}], "description": "Students learn how spreads, image scale, article lengths, and recurring features create momentum."}, {"id": "d004d54c-6ec9-4ce1-8044-6209e8a42529", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Navigation systems", "children": [{"id": "946a3523-72b7-4eff-bad0-b7d933031df6", "type": "concept", "title": "folios"}, {"id": "6cf477f8-434e-4133-a974-6490d2b0dfc6", "type": "concept", "title": "running heads"}, {"id": "99bd76b1-3a73-4f87-b2c9-8e306d522bb8", "type": "concept", "title": "section labels"}, {"id": "bcd40111-102f-44c9-b7de-54c3954876dc", "type": "concept", "title": "cross-references and anchors"}], "description": "Students design wayfinding devices that help readers understand where they are."}]}, {"id": "16ecde69-de40-470f-a45b-8abf08923a7e", "type": "topic", "title": "Print Production: Preflight, Packaging, PDFs, Imposition, and Proofing", "description": "This production unit prepares students to deliver files that printers and collaborators can actually use. The emphasis is accuracy, accountability, and proofing.", "children": [{"id": "daf267e7-16f5-4102-9031-a19b0567ab30", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Preflight and error correction", "children": [{"id": "66ae137d-8a92-4a8d-a3ca-19ad7674a7a2", "type": "concept", "title": "overset text"}, {"id": "cf00c974-9609-4ed4-a7ae-c620b7045ab0", "type": "concept", "title": "missing links and fonts"}, {"id": "32ccbb57-0682-4e3e-ba39-e95b64523f58", "type": "concept", "title": "low-resolution images"}, {"id": "b25855ba-8d69-4c49-bd35-b5725bfe7f1d", "type": "concept", "title": "bleed and color warnings"}], "description": "Students learn to catch problems before they become expensive output failures."}, {"id": "5d88c7f7-0636-4f98-9eaa-60d271e00613", "type": "subtopic", "title": "PDF export and packaging", "children": [{"id": "3019668b-7bdc-4ef4-885d-2d2963af7889", "type": "concept", "title": "PDF presets"}, {"id": "3e2964d6-0a6c-4971-999f-ea6454c0790e", "type": "concept", "title": "marks and bleeds"}, {"id": "09aab47f-37e2-4448-b7f3-6298111fb28b", "type": "concept", "title": "font embedding"}, {"id": "38bc4548-780d-4188-b7b8-dd35614b6a8a", "type": "concept", "title": "package folders"}], "description": "Students learn the difference between working files, proof PDFs, and press-ready PDFs."}, {"id": "76971afe-37f5-4556-ba81-e8428966e71d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Proofing and printer communication", "children": [{"id": "f7ca8a82-0faf-4266-9a66-c69e8357dd41", "type": "concept", "title": "soft proofing"}, {"id": "4e91a1d5-535f-4fb5-9a7e-c0bd111ebcb6", "type": "concept", "title": "hard proofs"}, {"id": "69d45477-bd42-4394-a2af-c32e8fd57717", "type": "concept", "title": "paper and binding specs"}, {"id": "9bb17c12-b562-407c-9ad3-6a5d4c6c4aad", "type": "concept", "title": "change logs and approval checkpoints"}], "description": "Students learn how to review proofs and speak clearly with vendors."}]}, {"id": "c1f6c6c0-5be3-42a8-9a16-e3e35e80e7f6", "type": "topic", "title": "Digital Publishing: Interactive PDFs, EPUB Basics, Accessibility, and Screen Output", "description": "Modern page layout often leaves the printed page. Students learn how InDesign documents can become accessible PDFs, interactive screen documents, or digital publication prototypes.", "children": [{"id": "cb4ea61c-5213-4919-846f-c52175688cc5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Interactive PDF features", "children": [{"id": "e02ab6f3-b716-457d-bfb3-da407cc9a83a", "type": "concept", "title": "buttons and links"}, {"id": "5f46c321-895e-41ec-aed5-752febf75b96", "type": "concept", "title": "bookmarks"}, {"id": "6e57bed5-4fbd-4731-a7ef-c6d9ca235810", "type": "concept", "title": "forms basics"}, {"id": "c126b3fd-59ff-4d8c-9326-5e41b558e681", "type": "concept", "title": "presentation and portfolio PDFs"}], "description": "Students learn when interactivity helps readers and how to add it without clutter."}, {"id": "17545803-e983-4afd-973e-de872216ac2e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "EPUB and screen publication basics", "children": [{"id": "9d5c2cb0-366e-406f-bae4-3b4c303bdb79", "type": "concept", "title": "fixed-layout EPUB"}, {"id": "5c5efeb7-f6fa-41d8-a8ee-7bf26b7ceb7d", "type": "concept", "title": "export limitations"}, {"id": "0902baa2-26f0-46a6-bc96-6e6c2eaef3b4", "type": "concept", "title": "image and type scaling"}, {"id": "c969d724-c53d-40bd-8ee4-86c64c4cac5f", "type": "concept", "title": "screen-friendly spacing"}], "description": "Students understand the differences between fixed layout, reflowable reading, and responsive digital formats."}, {"id": "395c3ac8-e565-4581-a1e6-4fd889b741d0", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Accessibility and inclusive output", "children": [{"id": "e96dfbf0-5809-4d0d-ab89-7541fc6c1cce", "type": "concept", "title": "reading order"}, {"id": "b3598cc1-87ea-44be-a9fb-164d159a03e8", "type": "concept", "title": "alt text"}, {"id": "9ccc6535-fa2e-479d-b9d3-7eeb8344bff9", "type": "concept", "title": "tagged PDFs"}, {"id": "1d58bc4d-1544-46d0-8e7c-d32877f44959", "type": "concept", "title": "color contrast and type size"}], "description": "Students learn to design files that can be read by more people and reviewed against accessibility expectations."}]}, {"id": "8076be1a-7a37-4795-bcf1-8d4338819742", "type": "topic", "title": "Editorial Systems: Magazines, Lookbooks, Reports, Books, and Brand Publications", "description": "Students apply layout principles to real publication genres. The goal is to understand the conventions, risks, and opportunities of each format.", "children": [{"id": "e86786d2-7722-439b-ada9-684b4b559dad", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Magazine and editorial formats", "children": [{"id": "cac1d047-b181-451c-9921-f692b6cf9d2d", "type": "concept", "title": "cover lines and mastheads"}, {"id": "772eccb2-6411-4b1b-be95-33e2c5166ac0", "type": "concept", "title": "departments and feature wells"}, {"id": "25bb3889-24e1-4e43-94ba-ecb665bb6cc6", "type": "concept", "title": "image-led storytelling"}, {"id": "ebcb471b-1c8e-4024-ba6b-c7e753c3f64b", "type": "concept", "title": "advertising and sponsored content"}], "description": "Students learn how recurring departments, features, covers, and advertising constraints shape editorial design."}, {"id": "683a77f2-9725-4d5b-b756-661348cfbb40", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Reports and information-heavy documents", "children": [{"id": "6154830a-3d20-4d47-a696-fdaeeb59e25f", "type": "concept", "title": "executive summaries"}, {"id": "02f3fc91-c84c-4e11-a5d1-408648444a66", "type": "concept", "title": "charts and tables"}, {"id": "b7426ca1-6d18-4b96-be90-cdb346dafc43", "type": "concept", "title": "data callouts"}, {"id": "eba6a860-23e5-4d62-af8b-897a9e431908", "type": "concept", "title": "appendices and references"}], "description": "Students learn to organize dense information so audiences can scan, trust, and act on it."}, {"id": "5c8edcbe-8f73-48bd-9ec9-afb55c662917", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Books, catalogs, and brand publications", "children": [{"id": "5ec6c4a8-e85d-4312-bf68-c126d05a0f59", "type": "concept", "title": "front and back matter"}, {"id": "f6d633d3-a5a7-45bc-b376-b7db257b6bd4", "type": "concept", "title": "lookbooks and catalogs"}, {"id": "b3793763-961d-4740-8053-8bde9c9f9044", "type": "concept", "title": "brand guidelines in layout"}, {"id": "12011e29-8b3a-46e9-8afc-2ffd08204f28", "type": "concept", "title": "series and volume logic"}], "description": "Students practice longer systems where rhythm, durability, and brand consistency matter."}]}, {"id": "925be4a7-8e01-434a-9ff5-94129fe7d06d", "type": "topic", "title": "Collaboration, Version Control, Client Review, and Production Handoff", "description": "This unit focuses on the realities of professional work: feedback, deadlines, versioning, review rounds, and handoff expectations.", "children": [{"id": "b167d271-c016-4093-9577-294c1cd1694a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Version and file management", "children": [{"id": "e6f2d846-b747-4526-9118-2e0bb8455170", "type": "concept", "title": "version naming"}, {"id": "aef19706-0933-45cb-911e-05afe807140c", "type": "concept", "title": "archive folders"}, {"id": "3d463121-45c1-42df-bc94-c356f9d7811c", "type": "concept", "title": "linked asset stability"}, {"id": "b605647f-3ab9-40ba-bea4-d51f40904b0a", "type": "concept", "title": "change summaries"}], "description": "Students learn how to keep work traceable across critiques, client reviews, and production rounds."}, {"id": "bfb09327-4741-4cc2-ac69-b840ef76c3dd", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Review and annotation workflows", "children": [{"id": "fbd64686-1c00-4d6b-938d-d6132db86ac7", "type": "concept", "title": "PDF comments"}, {"id": "95e1aceb-8548-413d-b120-ad8c416e7bdc", "type": "concept", "title": "client notes"}, {"id": "e529e5cd-5fa4-4d61-9b2e-0a15ccdaf97a", "type": "concept", "title": "design rationale"}, {"id": "1ac0d7a4-857b-48d0-99ec-40bb21830631", "type": "concept", "title": "revision prioritization"}], "description": "Students learn how to receive, interpret, and resolve comments without losing design intent."}, {"id": "39e241d9-3b8c-4912-90e4-bdf6dfd4f3b4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Handoff packages", "children": [{"id": "83d9bb21-7006-46d6-b353-cd94f89977d7", "type": "concept", "title": "packaged InDesign files"}, {"id": "21eb1309-365d-4a78-b900-589bb04e8d1b", "type": "concept", "title": "final PDFs"}, {"id": "9b35d1cb-b7f4-4c5d-b198-34b4d01975f3", "type": "concept", "title": "source assets and licenses"}, {"id": "aa60ac27-a308-4ff1-adca-b50a8844db03", "type": "concept", "title": "readme and production notes"}], "description": "Students learn what a complete final delivery includes for printers, clients, and future designers."}]}, {"id": "63affcc8-9fbd-4e93-92ad-011998800349", "type": "topic", "title": "Critique, Revision, Quality Control, and Portfolio Documentation", "description": "Students learn to critique layout work with precision and to revise toward clearer communication, stronger craft, and better portfolio presentation.", "children": [{"id": "6efaf1b5-3830-4dde-9368-26a302fb9720", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Critique language", "children": [{"id": "3445fa30-b051-4268-8796-0f4d0595549b", "type": "concept", "title": "formal critique vocabulary"}, {"id": "c2d6fb91-561b-4c4d-bce9-20d95dc9954a", "type": "concept", "title": "reader-centered feedback"}, {"id": "c31022a4-6004-4a10-b0a7-04ddc77f47ee", "type": "concept", "title": "production critique"}, {"id": "ab70d1a9-5173-484b-881b-8ddb256eacf5", "type": "concept", "title": "self-assessment prompts"}], "description": "Students learn to discuss layout decisions in terms of hierarchy, audience, system, craft, and evidence."}, {"id": "4c3da9b5-edeb-4485-8c4c-59d5d34ebf68", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Revision strategy", "children": [{"id": "76b5d91f-d55a-4599-95a5-6869562c1545", "type": "concept", "title": "revision priorities"}, {"id": "d5dc242c-61ce-403a-91bc-977f27727077", "type": "concept", "title": "A/B layout variants"}, {"id": "8822d3f7-fb21-4f77-a12e-e3bf73a2d81d", "type": "concept", "title": "content and design tradeoffs"}, {"id": "474dc8d1-55af-4416-8107-dc6de8b1dd35", "type": "concept", "title": "before-and-after documentation"}], "description": "Students learn how to move from feedback to focused design iterations rather than endless polishing."}, {"id": "19441b9d-bf4a-4b2d-b897-b1697b7b61db", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Portfolio case documentation", "children": [{"id": "c7a43e73-a379-4616-ba3c-4108e86ebdae", "type": "concept", "title": "project brief"}, {"id": "e958835e-939e-41a7-8fcc-a620592409eb", "type": "concept", "title": "research and sketches"}, {"id": "7433088c-3320-4a91-b933-ff1e8b2e7ddb", "type": "concept", "title": "spread mockups"}, {"id": "7d6318bc-4994-4309-960d-840100245aa3", "type": "concept", "title": "final documentation and reflection"}], "description": "Students learn to present publication projects as process-rich design cases."}]}, {"id": "30349eb7-261b-4c71-9651-4be65efe8661", "type": "topic", "title": "Capstone Publication Project, Presentation, and Professional Pathways", "description": "The final unit synthesizes the course into a polished publication system and a professional presentation that shows both design thinking and production competence.", "children": [{"id": "9a50d2d0-9585-462a-80ee-689ea06c5d59", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Capstone brief and concept", "children": [{"id": "5c4c0f74-f652-4786-b354-9803a2b36095", "type": "concept", "title": "creative brief"}, {"id": "bc011836-010b-446e-a2d2-62e77cba980b", "type": "concept", "title": "audience research"}, {"id": "c7fe0df7-1270-4263-83d3-5c73aebcdca7", "type": "concept", "title": "content strategy"}, {"id": "031a22b6-3ab3-48cc-8862-cb447d89ee62", "type": "concept", "title": "visual direction"}], "description": "Students define a publication problem with audience, content, format, and production constraints."}, {"id": "720585e1-a608-4ca8-b3ad-8dda9e2cbf52", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Final publication system", "children": [{"id": "6dd5ada2-c4a4-4fbe-99d2-f87a14cb0e14", "type": "concept", "title": "cover and interior spreads"}, {"id": "08985916-d47f-43a2-9c95-46dba3a43381", "type": "concept", "title": "style sheets"}, {"id": "b4f4c38a-19ae-4afe-855f-3363dd8d136c", "type": "concept", "title": "image and asset system"}, {"id": "73ccfe26-57fa-443e-bef3-6184069bee94", "type": "concept", "title": "print and digital exports"}], "description": "Students produce a complete layout system that demonstrates hierarchy, pacing, styles, image control, and output readiness."}, {"id": "8d470d90-8311-49b3-9e2c-b61cb3e9c0db", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Professional presentation", "children": [{"id": "899192fd-cf72-4fa2-ab23-bd4e27f92851", "type": "concept", "title": "process narrative"}, {"id": "a79f6402-0fa5-4b65-8a2e-4e9d29d250c1", "type": "concept", "title": "print or mockup presentation"}, {"id": "38be798c-e406-43fc-996b-72a5f3f593cb", "type": "concept", "title": "digital PDF walkthrough"}, {"id": "538ce5b5-56b9-4ba3-9947-a58b0e9890a6", "type": "concept", "title": "career roles in editorial and production design"}], "description": "Students learn to present layout work as a coherent design argument and career-ready portfolio artifact."}]}], "dbBacked": true}$pagljson$::jsonb,
