roduction Handoff", "description": "This unit focuses on the realities of professional work: feedback, deadlines, versioning, review rounds, and handoff expectations.", "children": [{"id": "b167d271-c016-4093-9577-294c1cd1694a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Version and file management", "children": [{"id": "e6f2d846-b747-4526-9118-2e0bb8455170", "type": "concept", "title": "version naming"}, {"id": "aef19706-0933-45cb-911e-05afe807140c", "type": "concept", "title": "archive folders"}, {"id": "3d463121-45c1-42df-bc94-c356f9d7811c", "type": "concept", "title": "linked asset stability"}, {"id": "b605647f-3ab9-40ba-bea4-d51f40904b0a", "type": "concept", "title": "change summaries"}], "description": "Students learn how to keep work traceable across critiques, client reviews, and production rounds."}, {"id": "bfb09327-4741-4cc2-ac69-b840ef76c3dd", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Review and annotation workflows", "children": [{"id": "fbd64686-1c00-4d6b-938d-d6132db86ac7", "type": "concept", "title": "PDF comments"}, {"id": "95e1aceb-8548-413d-b120-ad8c416e7bdc", "type": "concept", "title": "client notes"}, {"id": "e529e5cd-5fa4-4d61-9b2e-0a15ccdaf97a", "type": "concept", "title": "design rationale"}, {"id": "1ac0d7a4-857b-48d0-99ec-40bb21830631", "type": "concept", "title": "revision prioritization"}], "description": "Students learn how to receive, interpret, and resolve comments without losing design intent."}, {"id": "39e241d9-3b8c-4912-90e4-bdf6dfd4f3b4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Handoff packages", "children": [{"id": "83d9bb21-7006-46d6-b353-cd94f89977d7", "type": "concept", "title": "packaged InDesign files"}, {"id": "21eb1309-365d-4a78-b900-589bb04e8d1b", "type": "concept", "title": "final PDFs"}, {"id": "9b35d1cb-b7f4-4c5d-b198-34b4d01975f3", "type": "concept", "title": "source assets and licenses"}, {"id": "aa60ac27-a308-4ff1-adca-b50a8844db03", "type": "concept", "title": "readme and production notes"}], "description": "Students learn what a complete final delivery includes for printers, clients, and future designers."}]}, {"id": "63affcc8-9fbd-4e93-92ad-011998800349", "type": "topic", "title": "Critique, Revision, Quality Control, and Portfolio Documentation", "description": "Students learn to critique layout work with precision and to revise toward clearer communication, stronger craft, and better portfolio presentation.", "children": [{"id": "6efaf1b5-3830-4dde-9368-26a302fb9720", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Critique language", "children": [{"id": "3445fa30-b051-4268-8796-0f4d0595549b", "type": "concept", "title": "formal critique vocabulary"}, {"id": "c2d6fb91-561b-4c4d-bce9-20d95dc9954a", "type": "concept", "title": "reader-centered feedback"}, {"id": "c31022a4-6004-4a10-b0a7-04ddc77f47ee", "type": "concept", "title": "production critique"}, {"id": "ab70d1a9-5173-484b-881b-8ddb256eacf5", "type": "concept", "title": "self-assessment prompts"}], "description": "Students learn to discuss layout decisions in terms of hierarchy, audience, system, craft, and evidence."}, {"id": "4c3da9b5-edeb-4485-8c4c-59d5d34ebf68", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Revision strategy", "children": [{"id": "76b5d91f-d55a-4599-95a5-6869562c1545", "type": "concept", "title": "revision priorities"}, {"id": "d5dc242c-61ce-403a-91bc-977f27727077", "type": "concept", "title": "A/B layout variants"}, {"id": "8822d3f7-fb21-4f77-a12e-e3bf73a2d81d", "type": "concept", "title": "content and design tradeoffs"}, {"id": "474dc8d1-55af-4416-8107-dc6de8b1dd35", "type": "concept", "title": "before-and-after documentation"}], "description": "Students learn how to move from feedback to focused design iterations rather than endless polishing."}, {"id": "19441b9d-bf4a-4b2d-b897-b1697b7b61db", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Portfolio case documentation", "children": [{"id": "c7a43e73-a379-4616-ba3c-4108e86ebdae", "type": "concept", "title": "project brief"}, {"id": "e958835e-939e-41a7-8fcc-a620592409eb", "type": "concept", "title": "research and sketches"}, {"id"